# Build context trimming. The core build needs source, cmake, deps and .git
# (for the revision header); it does not need 189MB of SQL, 24MB of runbook
# evidence, or any local build tree.
#
# Every pattern here is anchored at the context root -- `core/sql/` matches
# ./core/sql and nothing else. That mattered the moment the core moved into the
# core/ submodule (ADR-0020): upstream's world data went with it, so the 130MB
# this file exists to keep out of the context came back as core/sql/ and had to
# be named again. The same trap waits for anything added below: check whether
# the core has one too. There is deliberately no root `sql/` entry any more --
# that tree was a stale duplicate of core/sql and is gone; ops/audit/
# no-duplicate-core-sql.sh fails the build if one reappears.
runbooks/
core/sql/
docs/
core/docs/
patches/
ops/

# NOT ignored, and easy to add here by mistake: core/ itself, and .git. The
# builder stage does COPY . /src and configures the platform root, which
# FATAL_ERRORs if core/CMakeLists.txt is absent; and the revision header is
# produced by running git inside core/, which needs both core/.git (a file
# pointing into .git/modules/core) and .git itself.
**/build/
**/.vs/
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/CMakeFiles/
*.log

# ci.yml artefacts. The staged install (./stage) is deliberately NOT here - the
# ci-staged target COPYs it - but everything else the build job leaves behind is
# large and would only slow the context transfer down.
.ccache/
.sccache/
.vcpkg-cache/
.ci/
test-results/
image/

# Rendered runtime config and the environment it is rendered from. These are
# generated artefacts, never inputs to the image, and mangosd.conf carries the
# database password in cleartext:
#     LoginDatabaseInfo = "db;3306;turtle;<password>;tw_logon"
# The runtime stage only copies ${PREFIX}, so a released image is unaffected --
# but `COPY . /src` puts them in the BUILDER layer, and any pushed builder or
# cache image would carry the credential.
deploy/compose/config/
deploy/compose/.env
**/.env
